WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Does a plant really need sunlight if it already has water?

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:08.580
Four cups of radish seedlings and a dark cupboard give a fair answer.

3
00:00:11.683 --> 00:00:16.503
Setup takes about thirty minutes, then quick checks every day or two for about two

4
00:00:16.503 --> 00:00:20.423
weeks. Your child practices running a fair test.

5
00:00:21.543 --> 00:00:25.243
They make a guess, change one thing, and check the result over time.

6
00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:30.177
You need four small cups, with holes an adult pokes in the bottom.

7
00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.877
Add a tray, potting mix, and radish seeds.

8
00:00:35.157 --> 00:00:40.037
Bring water, a tablespoon, labels, and a cupboard or a big box for a dark place.

9
00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.980
Have an adult open the potting mix with scissors outdoors or by an open window.

10
00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.440
Keep your child back and turn your face away.

11
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.320
Dampen the mix before scooping to reduce dust.

12
00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.100
Read the seed packet and choose untreated seeds.

13
00:00:58.133 --> 00:01:03.473
Fill the four cups and label them: light plus water, dark plus water, light no

14
00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:04.773
water, dark no water.

15
00:01:06.013 --> 00:01:10.013
Your child presses four or five seeds into each cup and covers them.

16
00:01:11.213 --> 00:01:13.233
Give each cup two tablespoons of water.

17
00:01:14.317 --> 00:01:16.737
Keep all four cups on a sunny windowsill.

18
00:01:18.017 --> 00:01:21.077
When the top feels dry, water each cup the same amount.

19
00:01:22.437 --> 00:01:24.537
Sprouts usually appear in three to ten days.

20
00:01:25.837 --> 00:01:30.057
When most seedlings are about two centimeters tall, have your child predict what

21
00:01:30.057 --> 00:01:31.117
will happen to each cup.

22
00:01:32.457 --> 00:01:33.557
Write or draw their guesses.

23
00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:38.527
Use a cupboard free of cleaners that children cannot climb into.

24
00:01:39.887 --> 00:01:42.287
Move both dark cups inside and shut the door.

25
00:01:43.607 --> 00:01:46.747
Give each water cup two tablespoons when the top feels dry.

26
00:01:48.047 --> 00:01:49.507
Stop watering the other cups.

27
00:01:51.027 --> 00:01:53.927
Compare cups that differ only in light, or only in water.

28
00:01:55.017 --> 00:01:57.337
Picture the two cups that still get water.

29
00:01:58.677 --> 00:02:02.637
After about a week, how might the dark seedlings compare with the windowsill

30
00:02:02.637 --> 00:02:06.197
seedlings? Shorter, the same height, or taller?

31
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:15.100
The dark seedlings are often taller, thinner, and paler.

32
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.000
They may lean or flop as they stretch on stored food.

33
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.600
When you compare your cups, ask, 'What do you notice besides height?'

34
00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:28.310
Every day or two, take a quick look and return the dark cups.

35
00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:33.210
Draw each cup. Note height, color, and drooping.

36
00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.310
The dry cups usually droop within two to five days.

37
00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.950
Dark seedlings weaken over one to two weeks.

38
00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:44.590
The light and water cup stays green and upright.

39
00:02:45.683 --> 00:02:48.403
A green plant makes its own food in its leaves.

40
00:02:49.723 --> 00:02:52.323
It uses light, water, and a gas from the air.

41
00:02:53.603 --> 00:02:56.023
In the dark, a seedling lives on stored food.

42
00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.323
When that runs out, it cannot make more.

43
00:03:00.367 --> 00:03:02.927
Stay with your child while they plant and water.

44
00:03:04.327 --> 00:03:06.947
Nobody tastes the seeds, soil, or plants.

45
00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:11.447
Keep seeds and marker caps away from children under four.

46
00:03:12.627 --> 00:03:14.907
If a child is choking, call nine one one.

47
00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:20.307
Wash hands with soap and water after planting and after each check.

48
00:03:21.317 --> 00:03:24.297
At the end, lay the first guesses beside the cups.

49
00:03:25.697 --> 00:03:27.137
Ask, 'What surprised you?'

50
00:03:27.237 --> 00:03:29.997
Then ask, 'Where does a green plant get its food?'

51
00:03:30.717 --> 00:03:32.857
Let your child point to a cup as they explain.
